  "answer": "Fixed. `deleteFromCart` was sending the product's numeric **id** where the backend requires its **sku**.\n\n**Root cause:** The backend's only cart-item delete route is `DELETE /api/v1/cart/{code}/product/{sku}` (BasketEndpoint \u2192 `ShoppingCartFacade.removeShoppingCartItem(code, sku, \u2026)`), which identifies the line by its string `sku` (cart items are `ReadableShoppingCartItem`s, which inherit a `sku` field from `ProductEntity`). The action was building `cart/{cartID}/product/{item.id}` \u2014 the sku lookup never matched, the backend rejected the request (4xx), and since the error is swallowed in the `catch`, the `DELETE_FROM_CART` reducer never ran and the UI appeared to do nothing. Note the same file's `addToCart` already uses `item.sku` as the product identifier, so this was the inconsistent one.\n\n**Fix:** In [cartActions.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/okf/work/g1_delete_item/okf/codex/5/src/redux/actions/cartActions.js:163), changed the URL segment from `item.id` to `item.sku`. Only that file was modified.\n\n**Files consulted:**\n- `okf/index.md` and `okf/references/backend/routes.md` \u2014 found the delete route contract\n- `okf/references/backend/modules/com.salesmanager.shop.store.api.v1.shoppingCart.md` and `\u2026shoppingCart.facade.md` \u2014 confirmed the endpoint expects a sku string\n- `okf/references/backend/modules/com.salesmanager.shop.model.catalog.product.product.md` and `\u2026core.model.shoppingcart.md` \u2014 confirmed cart items carry a `sku`\n- `src/util/constant.js`, `src/util/webService.js`, `public/env-config.js` \u2014 confirmed the base URL produces `/api/v1/`\n- `src/pages/other/Cart.js` and `src/redux/reducers/cartReducer.js` \u2014 confirmed the call site and that the state update only happens on a successful HTTP call",
